==English==

===Verb===
'''to come across''' (third-person singular simple present '''[[comes across]]''', present participle '''[[coming across]]''', simple past '''[[came across]]''', past participle '''[[came across]]''')

# {{idiom}} To give an [[appearance]] or [[impression]]; to project a certain [[image]].	 
#:''A business suit and briefcase help her to '''come across''' as the competent professional she is.''
# To [[find]], usually by [[accident]].
#: ''In the meadow he will '''come across''' a rare flower.''